{
  "notes": [
    "Every vector is H_FIELDS_V1: preimage = u64_be(len(domain)) || domain || for each field u64_be(len(field)) || field; digest = SHA256(preimage).",
    "canonical TaskDataObjectRefV1 is the required nested eight-field frame task_hash, session_id, task_id, object_kind, content_hash, evidence_producer_kind, verify_round, optional producer_operator. Nexus transport carries Hash32 as lowercase hex, but the preimage always takes raw32.",
    "A non-evidence object pins evidence_producer_kind UNSPECIFIED, verify_round 0 and an absent producer_operator; the metadata and fetch vectors below exercise exactly that.",
    "A whole-object read signs range absent, which is the single byte 0x00, and must not be rewritten as a present range with zero offset and length. The fetch vector here carries a present range so both encodings are pinned.",
    "The two finalize signature digests are SHA256 over the raw 64-byte service signature, never over its hex text, so another signature cannot be substituted into an already authenticated body.",
    "task_data_request_v1_cortex_service embeds the digest of task_data_upload_body_v1 as its body_digest; the two are one chain and must be regenerated together. Only CORTEX_SERVICE uses this domain. The USER path signs the same ten values as EIP-712 v4 typed data under the TrueOpen Task Data Request domain and produces a keccak digest, so it is not an H_FIELDS_V1 vector and is not listed here.",
    "Each vector carries mutations[]: one per encodable leaf plus the semantic cases §10.1 names. A mutation only asserts the digest moves or the input is rejected; it never introduces a domain. digest_hex is the value the mutated input produces, so an implementation that ignores a field will reproduce the positive digest and fail here."
  ],
  "schema": "trueopen.task.data_auth.v1",
